<p>A Python package exposes the stages through one CLI; SLURM runs every heavy step. Scikit-learn, pydiffmap, GPyTorch and umap-learn supply the methods; Jinja2 and WeasyPrint render PDFs, checked with pypdf. There is no multi-agent framework, database or web service. Labels only stratify cohorts and color secondary plots.</p>

<h2>3 · Dataset-aware planning and decision logic</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Profile evidence</th><th>PBMC3k</th><th>PathMNIST</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Source size</td><td>{{ '{:,}'.format(P.profile.n_samples) }} × {{ '{:,}'.format(P.profile.n_features) }}</td><td>{{ '{:,}'.format(M.profile.n_samples) }} × {{ '{:,}'.format(M.profile.n_features) }}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sparsity · non-negative · integer · max</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(P.profile.statistics.sparsity) }} · {{ P.profile.statistics.nonnegative }} · {{ P.profile.statistics.integer_valued }} · {{ P.profile.statistics.max_value|int }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(M.profile.statistics.sparsity) }} · {{ M.profile.statistics.nonnegative }} · {{ M.profile.statistics.integer_valued }} · {{ M.profile.statistics.max_value|int }}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Branch chosen by rules</td><td><strong>count matrix</strong></td><td><strong>bounded intensity</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td>Executed steps (per cohort)</td><td>{% for a in P.plan.actions %}{{ a.action|replace('_', ' ') }}{% if not loop.last %} → {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td><td>{% for a in M.plan.actions %}{{ a.action|replace('_', ' ') }}{% if not loop.last %} → {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p><strong>Evidence.</strong> All ten methods receive the identical input: 1,000 observations and the first 50 principal components of the preprocessed features. Stochastic methods run with 3 seeds, and every method is refitted on the same 5 random 80% subsamples. Metrics are label-free and Euclidean in that input space:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>T</strong> (trustworthiness) and <strong>R</strong> (15-nearest-neighbor recall) measure local structure.</li>
<li><strong>G</strong> is the Spearman correlation of pairwise distances, a global measure.</li>
<li><strong>S</strong> is the kNN overlap between subsample refits, a stability measure that applies to deterministic and stochastic methods alike.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Q = 0.35 T + 0.35 R + 0.20 G + 0.10 S.</strong> A method is ineligible after a failure or a severe diagnostic: a disconnected or singular graph, a collapsed layout, a near-disconnected diffusion graph, or SMACOF reaching its iteration limit.</p>
<p><strong>Rules.</strong> PCA is kept as the linear baseline. Among the rest, a method is eligible if any of these holds:</p>
<ul>
<li>it reaches 90% of the best Q;</li>
<li>it is within a practical-equivalence margin of the best (max of 2 paired subsample SE and 0.005);</li>
<li>it lies on a quality–runtime frontier where runtime differences count only when they are at least 2× and at least 1 s.</li>
</ul>
<p>At most four methods advance, ranked by Q. Tuning, on the shortlist only, keeps the default unless another grid point beats it by more than the margin. The final size is the largest candidate whose conservatively projected cost fits a 30-minute per-run limit, a 40-minute stage budget and 24 GB of memory.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Implementation (pilot defaults)</th><th>Method</th><th>Implementation (pilot defaults)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>PCA</td><td>sklearn PCA (full SVD)</td><td>Laplacian</td><td>sklearn SpectralEmbedding (kNN 30)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Kernel PCA</td><td>sklearn KernelPCA (RBF, median γ)</td><td>Diffusion maps</td><td>pydiffmap (α 0.5, k 64, median ε)</td></tr>
<tr><td>MDS</td><td>sklearn metric SMACOF, classical start</td><td>GPLVM</td><td>GPyTorch Bayesian GPLVM (75 epochs)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Isomap</td><td>sklearn Isomap (k 15)</td><td>t-SNE</td><td>sklearn TSNE (perplexity 30, PCA init)</td></tr>
<tr><td>LLE</td><td>sklearn LLE (k 20, reg 1e-3)</td><td>UMAP</td><td>umap-learn (k 15, min_dist 0.1)</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<h2>4 · Results</h2>
<figure><img src="reports/source/figures/pilot_quality_both.png"><figcaption>Figure 2. Pilot quality of all ten methods on each dataset. Open circles are ineligible because of a severe diagnostic. Full per-method evidence is in generated_report_1.pdf and generated_report_2.pdf.</figcaption></figure>
